WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
- [Narrator] This is the exclusive

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.570
trillion dollar company club.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.810
It's made up of some of
tech's biggest giants,

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:11.310
and for a moment, on May
30th, this company, Nvidia.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.670
It's not a household name,
but one day in late May,

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.670
Nvidia added nearly $184
billion in market value.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.010
That's a single day sum worth
more than other companies

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:26.250
in the semiconductor
industry, and just a fraction

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.810
of its total value.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.420
The company's record
sales have been fueled

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:32.220
by an emerging technology.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:34.710
- We're the world's engine for AI.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.330
- [Narrator] Here's how an under-the-radar

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:40.350
graphics processor is
cashing in on the AI craze

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.633
and what's next for its strategy.

00:00:43.665 --> 00:00:44.498
- [Character] Excellent.

00:00:44.498 --> 00:00:47.400
- [Narrator] When Nvidia
was founded in 1993,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.440
it established itself as a leader

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.440
in graphic processing units,
or GPUs, for video games.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:57.120
The company's powerful
chips made images crisper

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.260
and less choppy.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.666
- Nature of our technology

00:00:59.666 --> 00:01:04.666
is to accelerate multimedia
applications for the consumer.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.300
- [Narrator] In the years since,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.880
the company's chips have
become an indispensable part

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.880
of many other products,
from PCs to cars to robots.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.413
Nvidia made a pivotal decision in 2006

00:01:16.413 --> 00:01:18.930
when it started allowing
software developers

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.520
to play with its GPUs.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.670
- If you want to be a
trillion dollar company,

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.719
you can't do just one thing,
kind of like opening a door.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:30.480
And once they opened that
door, people started to tinker.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.860
- [Narrator] One of those expansions

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.720
was cryptocurrency mining.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.540
The company's GPUs could
handle the large amount

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:39.570
of computational power the task required.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.430
Business flourished.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.470
Rising sales from the crypto rush

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.870
helped Nvidia pass rival Intel

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.060
in market value in 2020.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.250
But sales fell as crypto crashed

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.960
and the gaming industry slumped.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.790
Still, the chip maker was starting

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:57.900
to see another frontier
boom: generative AI.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.640
In May, sales of chips

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:04.080
for the data centers needed
to power AI were up by 14%,

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.970
thanks in large part to the growing need

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:09.270
for Nvidia chips in AI calculations.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.390
For Nvidia, that was a
decade in the making.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:15.360
The company's chips broke
through in the AI community

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.110
in 2012 with a neural
network called AlexNet.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.530
- We saw early on about a decade or so ago

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.680
that this way of doing software
could change everything.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:26.820
- It was very futuristic.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.740
It was very uncertain at that point.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.320
Nobody knew how big AI was gonna be.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.660
They made that big bet
at a time when a lot

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:35.970
of other competitors were
not making that kind of bet.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:40.110
- We risked everything
to pursue deep learning.

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.870
- [Narrator] Nvidia chips
are suited for powering AI

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:44.610
because of their ability to do lots

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:47.220
of complex computations simultaneously.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.730
Traditional processing units
can't do that as quickly.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.720
And other GPUs, like
those from Intel and AMD,

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.750
haven't gained major market
share in AI computing.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:01.230
- If you think about how
graphics work, your monitor,

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.930
your computer monitor has a lot of pixels,

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.490
thousands of pixels on it,

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.273
and your computer needs to calculate

00:03:07.273 --> 00:03:09.690
at any given time what each

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.430
of those pixels need to look like.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:14.640
It was discovered fairly
quickly after Nvidia kind

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.130
of opened up the door for
people to use its chips

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.160
for other things that they
were actually really good

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.320
at the kind of mathematics

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.750
that underpins artificial intelligence.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.640
- [Narrator] In late 2022,

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.310
AI exploded with the public release

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:34.310
of OpenAI's ChatGPT and
Nvidia's stock skyrocketed.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.930
While companies like Google, Microsoft,

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:40.320
and Amazon battle it out in the AI race,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.050
Nvidia is raking in the cash.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:46.110
That's because its chips
power most of them.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.520
- For Nvidia, it's a bonanza.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:51.420
All of these folks who are
competing to get a slice

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.960
of the generative AI pie need Nvidia.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.480
- [Narrator] In 2018,
the division that focuses

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:00.240
on AI computation made up less than half

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.710
of the company's sales.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:04.410
By 2022, it was the majority.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.720
- It went from Wall Street
expectation of 7 billion

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.120
to Nvidia saying actually
gonna make 11 billion.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.830
And so that really opened people's eyes.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:13.740
It was a real statement that, you know,

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:16.770
this generative AI craze that
everybody's talking about

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.870
is more than just a hype cycle.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:19.830
- [Narrator] But that success

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:21.540
is creating a different problem

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.190
for the company: supply.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:27.810
- The demand is literally from
every corner of the world.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:31.530
- GPUs are at this point
considerably harder

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:32.694
to get than drugs.

00:04:32.694 --> 00:04:34.200
(Elon chuckling)

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.760
- [Narrator] The company's supply chain

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.827
hasn't been able to keep pace.

00:04:37.827 --> 00:04:39.870
- The the chip manufacturing cycle is such

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:41.490
that you can't just immediately make more

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.950
of these things like
today if you want them.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.860
- The company says it has
filled out some of its supply.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:50.700
- [Colette] We are working
on both supply today

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:51.870
for this quarter

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:55.050
but we have also procured
a substantial amount

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:57.060
of supply for the second half.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:58.530
- [Narrator] But the chip's global demand

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.030
has also caught the company

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:02.100
in the crosshairs of increasing tensions

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.020
between the US and China.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:07.290
Last year, the company said $400 million

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:09.900
of its quarterly sales could be subject

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:13.080
to new US chip licensing
requirements for China.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.200
In response, Nvidia began
offering an alternative chip

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.730
to customers in China.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.590
Despite some roadblocks,

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:23.130
the chip industry has its
eyes on Nvidia's success.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.330
- They're still riding this boom.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.280
It's no nowhere near done.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.070
The real question is whether companies

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:32.340
can build huge, huge
businesses that are based

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:35.107
on that artificial
intelligence capability.

00:05:35.107 --> 00:05:37.774
(pensive music)

